{"ts": "2026-08-17T11:24:32Z", "agent": "claude", "seq": 67, "kind": "tool_result", "text": "  for `tasks.json`. Created on first write if missing (AC7).\n- `backend/tests/conftest.py` \u2014 set the data-file env var to a `pytest`\n  tmp path **before** `from app.main import app` runs (line 9), since that\n  import is what constructs the module-level `store` singleton and its\n  path is fixed at construction time. Without this, tests would load from\n  and write to the real data file.\n- `backend/tests/test_persistence.py` (new file, since this concern isn't\n  a single route \u2014 no natural `test_<route>.py` fit) \u2014 covers: state\n  surviving across two `TaskStore` instances pointed at the same tmp path\n  (simulating a restart), missing file starts empty, corrupt/malformed\n  file starts empty, id counter continuing correctly after reload, and\n  directory auto-creation.\n- `.gitignore` \u2014 add `backend/data/` so persisted task data is never\n  committed.\n\nNot affected: `frontend/` (entire directory), `backend/app/models.py`.\n\n## Decisions made here (not left open)\n\n1. **Data file location:** `backend/data/tasks.json`, resolved relative to\n   `store.py`'s own location (`Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent /\n   \"data\" / \"tasks.json\"`) rather than the process's current working\n   directory \u2014 so it resolves the same way whether uvicorn is started from\n   `backend/` (per this project's README) or elsewhere.\n2. **Override mechanism:** an environment variable (e.g. `TASKS_DATA_FILE`)\n   overrides the default path when set. This is the hook `conftest.py`\n   uses to redirect tests to an isolated tmp path \u2014 without it, tests and\n   the real running server would contend for the same file.\n3. **Write strategy:** synchronous, full-snapshot write on every mutation\n   (serialize the whole task list to JSON and write it), matching this\n   store's already-small scale (in-memory dict, no batching elsewhere).\n   Chosen over a write-ahead/append log as the simplest thing that\n   satisfies the acceptance criteria \u2014 this store has never optimized for\n   write volume and shouldn't start here.\n4. **Corrupt-file handling:** any exception raised while reading or\n   parsing the file at startup (`FileNotFoundError`, `json.JSONDecodeError`,\n   or a shape mismatch such as the parsed value not being a list of\n   objects with the expected keys) is caught at load time and treated\n   identically to \"no file\" \u2014 start empty. This is one code path, not two,\n   since the request draws no distinction between \"missing\" and \"corrupt.\"\n\n## Edge cases\n\n- Missing file on startup \u2192 start empty (AC5).\n- Corrupt/unparseable JSON on startup \u2192 start empty (AC6).\n- Valid JSON but wrong top-level shape (object instead of array) \u2192 treated\n  as corrupt, start empty.\n- Valid JSON array but entries missing required fields or with the wrong\n  types \u2192 treated as corrupt, start empty (no per-entry salvage, per\n  non-goals).\n- Empty file (0 bytes) \u2192 invalid JSON, treated as corrupt, start empty.\n- `backend/data/` directory doesn't exist yet \u2192 created automatically on\n  first write (AC7), not just documented as a manual setup step.\n- Tasks loaded with non-contiguous ids (e.g. `1, 3, 7` after prior\n  deletes) \u2192 next created task gets `8`, not `4` or `1` (AC4).\n- Rapid restart immediately after a mutation \u2192 the file already reflects\n  it, since writes are synchronous per-request, not batched/delayed.\n- Running the test suite must never read or write\n  `backend/data/tasks.json` on a developer's machine, even if that file\n  already exists from a real run (AC8).\n\n## Open questions\n\nNone \u2014 the choices that would normally be open (file location, override\nmechanism, write strategy, corrupt-file handling) are resolved above under\n\"Decisions made here,\" since none of them changes this spec's scope and a\nreasonable default exists for each.", "meta": {"n