{"ts": "2026-08-17T11:26:13Z", "agent": "claude", "seq": 183, "kind": "tool_result", "text": "-  (a, b) => (a.priority === 'high' ? 0 : 1) - (b.priority === 'high' ? 0 : 1)\n-)\n-```\n-\n-`sortedTasks` (not `visibleTasks`) is what gets passed to `<TaskList>`,\n-directly after the existing filter step (`App.jsx:27-31`) \u2014 sort runs\n-*within* the already-filtered subset, satisfying AC7 (a high-priority Done\n-task must not jump into the Open view).\n-\n-`AddTask`'s `onAdd` callback extends to accept `priority`:\n-`onAdd={(title, priority) => run(() => api.createTask(title, priority))}`.\n-\n-`TaskList` gets a new prop:\n-`onPriorityChange={(id, priority) => run(() => api.setPriority(id, priority))}`,\n-wired identically to the existing `onComplete`/`onDelete`/`onUpdate` props\n-(`App.jsx:51-56`).\n-\n-## `App.css` additions\n-\n-```css\n-.priority-select {\n-  padding: 0.4rem 0.6rem;\n-  border: 1px solid #ccd2d6;\n-  border-radius: 5px;\n-  background: #fff;\n-  color: #16191c;\n-  font: inherit;\n-  font-size: 0.85rem;\n-  cursor: pointer;\n-}\n-\n-.priority-select.priority-high {\n-  background: #a8480a;\n-  border-color: #a8480a;\n-  color: #fff;\n-}\n-\n-.priority-select.priority-low {\n-  background: #e8eaec;\n-  color: #4a545c;\n-}\n-\n-/* .priority-normal intentionally has no override \u2014 it is the baseline\n-   .priority-select styling above, so it blends into the row rather than\n-   drawing the eye, same as everything that isn't flagged high. */\n-```\n-\n-`.priority-select` base rule reuses the app's existing border color\n-(`#ccd2d6`, already used by `.add-task input` and `.task-title-input`) and\n-border-radius (`5px`, used everywhere else in the file) \u2014 no new geometry\n-introduced. Approximate rendered height with this padding + 1px border +\n-default line-height \u2248 30\u201332px, in line with the existing `Done`/`Delete`\n-buttons' ~34\u201336px (round 2's design note) \u2014 close enough not to look\n-mismatched in the row, and clears the ~24px minimum target size guidance.\n-\n-## States\n-\n-### Populated \u2014 the spec's own AC5 example\n-\n-Input order `[A:normal, B:high, C:low, D:high, E:normal]`, Open filter (or\n-All), rendered order `[B, D, A, C, E]`:", "meta": {"native_type": "user", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01ByYpBnbmC2gwJ5DmmCiWvj", "session_id": "06a04b86-59b4-4030-b9ec-a0f1ea773699"}}
