call `_save()` concurrently and race on the shared `.tmp` file / `os.replace`. This was already raised and explicitly deferred as a follow-up in the prior round (noted in this round's build handoff as \"#4, not addressed\"), and the spec's non-goal (\"no multi-process/multi-worker locking... this app runs as a single process\") only strictly rules out multi-*process* races, not multi-*thread* ones \u2014 worth a sentence in a follow-up ticket rather than blocking this cycle on it.\n\n**Verified:** `python3 -m pytest -q` \u2192 30 passed (same run I did in this review). Load/save round-trip, missing/corrupt/wrong-shape/empty-file handling, id-continuation after reload, and directory auto-creation are all covered by `backend/tests/test_persistence.py` and match spec ACs 1\u20138. Reviewed disk state before/after \u2014 nothing left in the tree by this review pass.\n\nVERDICT: changes-requested", "meta": {"native_type": "result", "subtype": "success", "session_id": "06a04b86-59b4-4030-b9ec-a0f1ea773699", "is_error": false, "total_cost_usd": 0.9526017000000001}}
